# Cloudflare Workers Assets header rules.
#
# Content-Type is set per-page rather than with a /* wildcard on purpose: a
# wildcard would also stamp text/html onto styles.css, script.js and every
# image under /img/, breaking them. Each HTML route is listed explicitly.
#
# Charset belongs in the header (not just the <meta> tag) because the HTTP
# header wins over the document when the two disagree, and crawlers that read
# headers only will otherwise have to guess the encoding.

/
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

/menus/
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

